{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340696",
      "title": "Using Middleware",
      "lectureOrder": 155,
      "videoOrder": 143,
      "sourceHash": "d38c24b25a8eb034fccc429c2c95023509767ce4f8fa13be2d71e3773dc7f3ce",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 4.32,
          "en": "So route handlers can be a useful feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.32,
          "end": 9.09,
          "en": "Another feature that can be useful is middleware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.09,
          "end": 10.83,
          "en": "and that is a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.83,
          "end": 14.37,
          "en": "that does actually not use the app folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "Instead, you set up middleware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "by going to your route project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "and then there next to the package.json file and so on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 28.08,
          "en": "you add a file named middleware.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.08,
          "end": 30.873,
          "en": "And again, that is a reserved file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.01,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "The position also is important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "it should be in the root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "In there, you should export a function called middleware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 43.95,
          "en": "and that function name is also important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.95,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "and that will now get a request object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 50.22,
          "en": "passed in automatically by NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.22,
          "end": 52.74,
          "en": "just as the route handler did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.74,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "And you then have to return a Next response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 60.963,
          "en": "which is something that must be imported from next/server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.1,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "And this next response thing here has various",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "methods you can call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "You can also instantiate it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 71.64,
          "en": "to create a new response from scratch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.64,
          "end": 75.36,
          "en": "but you get some utility methods like next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.36,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "which simply forwards the incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "to its actual destination.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "And that also kind of describes what the purpose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 88.743,
          "en": "of this middleware function is, as does its name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "It is a function that's not really meant to block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 99.38,
          "en": "or handle an incoming request, though you could do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 101.61,
          "en": "but instead it's typically meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.61,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "to take a look at some incoming request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 108.12,
          "en": "maybe change it a bit, maybe block it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.12,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "for example, to implement authentication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "and maybe redirect to another page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.21000000000001,
          "en": "if a user is not authenticated, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.21000000000001,
          "end": 120.42,
          "en": "which you could do with help of the built-in redirect method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 121.953,
          "en": "on this next response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 127.44,
          "en": "But you often also just might want to let the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.44,
          "end": 130.47,
          "en": "go on to its original destination,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 130.47,
          "end": 133.383,
          "en": "maybe after evaluating or changing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.33,
          "end": 137.79,
          "en": "So here again, we can lock that request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.79,
          "end": 141.09,
          "en": "to see what's inside, because here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.09,
          "end": 143.94,
          "en": "we don't really need that middleware feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.94,
          "end": 147.66,
          "en": "but it is another feature that is related to routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.66,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "which is why I wanted to introduce you to it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "because middleware does allow you to set up code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 157.17000000000002,
          "en": "that will run on every request that's sent to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.17000000000002,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "any page or any route anywhere in your entire website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 165.51,
          "en": "so that you can inspect that request block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.51,
          "end": 169.083,
          "en": "or redirect the request or do whatever you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "So here with that setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "if I save that and I open up that terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "where my server side code runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 181.59,
          "en": "and I clear it and restart that development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.59,
          "end": 185.52,
          "en": "so that we start with a clear output again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.52,
          "end": 188.25,
          "en": "If I load the news page, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.25,
          "end": 191.7,
          "en": "you see a request object was locked here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.7,
          "end": 194.49,
          "en": "but in there you actually see that it was not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "for the news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 197.703,
          "en": "but instead for the fav icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.38,
          "end": 200.73,
          "en": "Well, that's just the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.73,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "because when I visit this news page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "actually multiple requests are sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 207.93,
          "en": "and the fav icon request is one of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.93,
          "end": 210.96,
          "en": "But there also would be a request for every single image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "that's shown on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 215.53300000000002,
          "en": "because that also is loaded from our server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.53300000000002,
          "end": 218.55,
          "en": "and that also is done through a separate request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.55,
          "end": 221.55,
          "en": "And if you would scroll all the way up in your output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.55,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "you would also find the request for the news page somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 228.15,
          "en": "Here it is in my case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.15,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "And that shows you how that middleware function works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "It really runs this code for every request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 237.84300000000002,
          "en": "so that you can do with it whatever you want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 243.57,
          "en": "Now, you can also export a config object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 245.73,
          "en": "and this must be a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.73,
          "end": 249.84,
          "en": "or constant called config, which must be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 252.81,
          "en": "And in there you can set up a matcher property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.81,
          "end": 255.06,
          "en": "which must be called matcher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 255.06,
          "end": 259.65,
          "en": "and that would allow you to filter the kind of requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.65,
          "end": 261.123,
          "en": "that trigger the middleware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 266.16,
          "en": "For example, if I filter for /news here like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.16,
          "end": 268.62,
          "en": "and I then reload this page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.62,
          "end": 271.86,
          "en": "and I take another look at my server log thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 276.347,
          "en": "you would see that now there is this request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.47,
          "end": 281.34000000000003,
          "en": "for the news page, but I don't see the request for this icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.34000000000003,
          "end": 283.53,
          "en": "or for all those images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.53,
          "end": 286.29,
          "en": "So you could set up some filters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.29,
          "end": 288.45,
          "en": "And this does not just allow you to filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.45,
          "end": 289.92,
          "en": "for a single page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.92,
          "end": 291.87,
          "en": "but you can also filter for other pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.87,
          "end": 294.84000000000003,
          "en": "by setting up a more complex matcher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.84000000000003,
          "end": 297.69,
          "en": "And you can find all the details about this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 301.08,
          "en": "matcher configuration in the official documentation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.08,
          "end": 304.53,
          "en": "and you find a link to that attached so that you can learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.53,
          "end": 307.02,
          "en": "how you could set up this matcher, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.02,
          "end": 308.1,
          "en": "by passing an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.1,
          "end": 311.79,
          "en": "and using placeholders to match multiple routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.79,
          "end": 314.34,
          "en": "and not just a single route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.34,
          "end": 316.23,
          "en": "So that's something you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.23,
          "end": 317.52,
          "en": "And in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 317.52,
          "end": 321,
          "en": "this middleware feature is a feature you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321,
          "end": 324.21,
          "en": "to handle different requests differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.21,
          "end": 326.52,
          "en": "to inspect all kinds of requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.52,
          "end": 330,
          "en": "and potentially to also redirect requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330,
          "end": 333.99,
          "en": "depending on what you need to do in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.99,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "Here we don't really need that feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 338.613,
          "en": "but it's still important to know about it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
